CITY ATTORNEY’S OFFICE
MUNICIPAL BUILDING
2101 O’NEIL AVENUE, ROOM 308
CHEYENNE, WYOMING 82001
TELEPHONE: (307) 637-6306 | FACSIMILE: (307) 637-6373

MEMORANDUM

To:
 Honorable Mayor Patrick Collins and Members of the City Council

From:
John Brodie, Deputy City Attorney

Date:
May 17, 2023

Subject:
Ordinance creating Chapter 2.96, Ethical Obligations of Public Officials, Public
Members and City Employees, of Title 2, Administration and Personnel, specifying
the ethical duties and obligations of public officials, public members and employees
of the City of Cheyenne.

This ordinance is being proposed in accordance with Wyoming Statute 15-1-127(c), which
requires the governing body of each city and town, by ordinance, to "prescribe requirements
governing conflicts of interest by any employee and any member of his immediate family and
procedures by which any employee and any member of his immediate family may be exempt from
those requirements." The proposed ordinance also prescribes requirements and procedures
governing: (1) Public officials who have a personal or private interest in a matter under
consideration by the city council; and (2) Public members who have a conflict of interest with
respect to any proposed transaction, contract, policy, program or other matter under consideration
by the public member in their official capacity.

This proposal borrows language and concepts promulgated by the City of Casper under
Chapter 2.60 (Code of Ethics) of the city's municipal code. A copy of Chapter 2.60 is attached to
this memorandum for your review and consideration.
```

